From: Ubuntu gts9uwifi port contributors <gts9uwifi@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci: say why a system suspend is refused

On the SM-X910 in USB host role, xhci_suspend() returns -EINVAL because
its root hubs are not in HC_STATE_SUSPENDED, and the only trace is the PM
core's "platform_pm_suspend returns -22".  Log both root hub states
when that happens, to find out why they were not suspended.

Signed-off-by: Ubuntu gts9uwifi port contributors <gts9uwifi@example.com>

---
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
@@ -960,8 +960,14 @@
 		return 0;
 
 	if (hcd->state != HC_STATE_SUSPENDED ||
-	    (xhci->shared_hcd && xhci->shared_hcd->state != HC_STATE_SUSPENDED))
+	    (xhci->shared_hcd && xhci->shared_hcd->state != HC_STATE_SUSPENDED)) {
+		/* Name the culprit: the caller only sees -EINVAL. */
+		xhci_warn(xhci, "suspend refused: root hub states %d/%d (want %d)\n",
+			  hcd->state,
+			  xhci->shared_hcd ? xhci->shared_hcd->state : -1,
+			  HC_STATE_SUSPENDED);
 		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	/* Clear root port wake on bits if wakeup not allowed. */
 	xhci_disable_hub_port_wake(xhci, &xhci->usb3_rhub, do_wakeup);
